This repository is an independent reimplementation — for the DeepSeek Harness
(DSH) — of the multi-agent research protocol described by the MISAKA project.
It contains no MISAKA source code and no copied MISAKA documentation text.

Attribution to the design origin, as Apache License 2.0 section 4(d) requires
for redistributed works and derivative works:

    MISAKA
    Copyright 2026 Luciole Studio
    https://github.com/Luciole-Studio/Misaka-Agent
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

What was studied (public documentation only): the seven-stage node protocol
(plan → task cards → synthesis → red team → response → divergence review →
fork decision), the rule that an external coding agent ("ally") may take a
task card but never a review card, the layered-reconciliation vocabulary
(convergence / divergence / resonance / appropriation / displacement), and
the artifact set (plan, cards, synthesis revisions, review, divergence,
decision, SOURCES, errata).

What was deliberately not carried over: the panel/TUI, the LCM compression
engine, the PageIndex document engine and its OCR/DjVu/LibreOffice pipeline,
model-provider routing, automatic git commits, and the setup wizard.

